From 84c1c99d8c824c0a9da74b71b4d98638269f81cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:42:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): count admitted and interrupted owner-loss spend
 [daveey]

Address review 5998995314 on PR #3819. Owner-unavailable is a failure-budget
booking, not proof no turn ran: it also covers midrun interruptions. A
submitter's rc 69 can likewise lose an admission answer after a turn ran.
Exclude only owner_unavailable/owner_down or integer rc-69 crashes with no
owner_admitted event, no usage receipt, and no host_refusal except preadmission.
Count startup, midrun, unknown or malformed refusal proofs conservatively.

Five whys: the original failure counter fix changed dispatch, while spend
reads task_runs separately; the first exclusion reused failure outcomes;
those outcomes cover both preturn and midturn owner faults; lost receipts
can hide a real admitted turn; synthetic outcome-only fixtures missed the
admission and proof-phase boundary. The repair checks those independent
receipts and exercises the real dead-worker sweep.

RED on d78924ea6f: all 11 new negative cases fail (3 reviewer sweep probes,
8 evidence cases). GREEN: 9 importing test files, 206 passed; scripts/check
--base origin/main: 21 checks ok. Existing 8-real + 7-refusal acceptance now
uses the actual preadmission metadata shapes. Unadmitted refusal streak
remains excluded; cache-read tokens and reported <= runs remain intact.
